 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The usted command",
     "texto": [
      "To give directions, the **usted** command uses the subjunctive form:\n\n- **-ar → -e**: girar → **gire**, tomar → **tome**.\n- **-er / -ir → -a**: seguir → **siga**, coger → **coja**.\n\nFor **ustedes**, add **-n**: **sigan**, **giren**.\n\nThe negative command always uses that same form: **no gire** (usted), **no gires** (tú). After **no**, you do not use **gira**.\n\nWith an irregular verb, start from **yo**: sigo → **siga**. And some letters change to keep the sound: cruzar → **cruce**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Tú, usted and ustedes",
     "texto": [
      "Compare the three forms of a command, affirmative and negative:\n\n- **girar**: tú **gira** / **no gires** · usted **gire** / **no gire** · ustedes **giren** / **no giren**.\n- **seguir**: tú **sigue** / **no sigas** · usted **siga** / **no siga** · ustedes **sigan** / **no sigan**.\n- **cruzar**: tú **cruza** / **no cruces** · usted **cruce** / **no cruce** · ustedes **crucen** / **no crucen**.\n\nOnly the affirmative command with **tú** is different (**gira**, **sigue**, **cruza**). All the others use the **-e / -a** form."
     ],
